<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    The hardened runtime (required for notarization) enables library
    validation: the process may only dlopen libraries signed with OUR Team
    ID or by Apple. Bakin's media store loads sharp's npm-published native
    prebuild (signed by the sharp project), so without this entitlement the
    signed release binary refuses it at dlopen:
      "code signature ... not valid for use in process: mapping process and
       mapped file (non-platform) have different Team IDs"
    (margo, v0.0.1-rc.33, 2026-09-21). Standard posture for apps that load
    third-party native modules; notarization accepts it. Locally compiled
    dev binaries are unsigned, so ONLY the signed release artifact exhibits
    the failure — test coverage cannot catch a regression here, keep this
    file and the --entitlements flag paired.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
